Z||000000||bocefas||11-04-2001||08:57 PM||||It just so happens that the other day when I filled up with gas, my Odometer was on 69,200 miles...I fill up and hit my tripmeter, as usual...2 days later my tripmeter says 84 miles and my Odometer says 69,278 miles...Hmmm<P>So anyway I started to watch my odometer closely when I'm driving, and sure enough, every so often, usually when the tenths are like on 2 or 3, the odometer reverses and goes backward until the tenths are on zero, then it goes normally again.  It seems to happen more often at slower speeds.  Any ideas on what the deal is there?  And I hate to go anywhere to get it fixed, and have an "odometer discrepency" label slapped on my title.  I'm guessing that there's a worn gear somewhere on the back of the cluster or something like that, I've never had one apart so I'm pretty much shooting in the dark.  Any ideas would be helpful!||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||11-04-2001||09:09 PM||||When you re-zero the odometer you have to do it a couple of times to makes sure that the zeroes line up. I read if you don't do this you could damage the odometer. I also noticed that mine would not move sometimes if I didn't reset it right. Hope this helps<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
